hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1301","Bundar and Abu Musa narrated to us, they said: Mummal narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Alqamah, who is Ibn Marthad, on the authority of Sulayman bin Buraidah, on the authority of His father, H. Abu Ammar narrated to us, Waki’ bin Al-Jarrah narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Sinan, Abi Sinan Al-Shaybani, narrated to us, Salam bin Junada narrated to us, Waki` told us, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Sinan, on the authority of Alqamah ibn Marthad, on the authority of Sulayman ibn Buraydah, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed Peace be upon him, then a man said: Who called for the red camel? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I did not find that. Rather, mosques were built for what they were built for.” This is a comprehensive hadith"
